Rebrand the privileged content process label shown in task manager and about:processes from Mozilla to Pyxis.

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
The unified diff below is generated from the checkout and is applied with
  git apply gecko/patches/pyxis/<path>.PYXIS_DIFF
(or `patch -p1 <`). Everything above this line is rationale, not content;
git apply ignores it. Regenerate with scripts/regen-gecko-patches.sh.
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

diff --git a/toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/global/processTypes.ftl b/toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/global/processTypes.ftl
index 317d7d12d70d..e7f98cb77289 100644
--- a/toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/global/processTypes.ftl
+++ b/toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/global/processTypes.ftl
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ process-type-privilegedabout = Privileged About
 
 # process used to run privileged mozilla pages,
 # such as accounts.firefox.com
-process-type-privilegedmozilla = Privileged Mozilla Content
+process-type-privilegedmozilla = Privileged Pyxis Content
 
 process-type-extension = Extension
 
